    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 21 Castleland Park Drive is a spacious and recently built three-bedroom semi-detached home for sale in Balbriggan, extending to approximately 103 sq. m. Presented in excellent condition and recently painted internally, this energy-efficient property offers modern accommodation, off-street parking and a private west-facing rear garden that is not overlooked.\n\nSituated in a highly sought-after location within minutes of the M1 Motorway and approximately 15 minutes from Dublin Airport, the property will appeal to families, first-time buyers and commuters seeking a quality home close to Balbriggan`s many amenities.\n\nCastleland Park Drive is a prestigious and highly convenient Balbriggan address. The property is located within minutes of the M1 Motorway and approximately 15 minutes from Dublin Airport, making it an excellent choice for commuters. Balbriggan offers a wide range of shops, schools, leisure facilities, transport links and everyday amenities.\n\nThe ground floor comprises a welcoming entrance hall, a spacious front living room with double doors leading to the dining area, an open-plan kitchen and dining space with access to the rear garden, and a guest WC. Upstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, including a generous main bedroom with en-suite, together with a family bathroom and landing. The property also benefits from an installed alarm system and a water softener, helping to reduce limescale build-up and improve water quality throughout the home.\n\nBalbriggan itself is a vibrant coastal town undergoing transformation improvements, with 30 million being invested in the \"Our Balbriggan\" project to enhance the town centre, harbour, and surrounding areas. The nearby Irish Institute of Music & Song adds a unique cultural charm, while recreational facilities and scenic amenities make Balbriggan one of North County Dublin`s most desirable areas to live. Families will appreciate the variety of local primary and secondary schools, and the scenic Ardgillan Castle & Demesne is just a short drive away for weekend outings. Rich in history, Balbriggan has been one of the fastest growing towns in Ireland in recent years and has now one of the youngest populations.\n\nCombining an A-rated specification, generous accommodation and a private west-facing garden, No. 21 Castleland Park Drive is an exceptional three-bedroom semi-detached house for sale in Balbriggan.\n\nContact Halligan O`Connor, Balbriggan Estate Agents,to arrange a private viewing. \n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance - 2.2m (7'3\") x 5.26m (17'3\")\n\nLiving Room - 3.16m (10'4\") x 5.13m (16'10\")\n\nW/C - 1.44m (4'9\") x 1.45m (4'9\")\n\nDining Area - 3.58m (11'9\") x 4.17m (13'8\")\n\nKitchen - 2.9m (9'6\") x 5.78m (19'0\")\n\nLanding - 3.25m (10'8\") x 1.88m (6'2\")\n\nMain Bedroom - 4.15m (13'7\") x 3.75m (12'4\")\n\nEn Suite - 1.56m (5'1\") x 2m (6'7\")\n\nBathroom - 2.23m (7'4\") x 1.88m (6'2\")\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.26m (7'5\") x 3.1m (10'2\")\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.76m (9'1\") x 3.1m (10'2\")\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
